                <page>
                    <exercise>
                        <statement>
                            <p>
                                A population (in thousands) changes according to the updating function
<me>
    p_{t+1}= 2(p_{t})^{4}-8(p_{t})^{3}+10(p_{t})^{2} -3p_{t}.
</me>
The equilibrium values of this system are at <m>p^{*} =0</m>, <m>p^{*} = 1</m>, and <m>p^{*} = 2</m>. 
Write the updating function rule as “<m>f(x)=</m>”, then compute the derivative of the updating function rule.
Use the Stability Theorem to classify each equilibrium value as "stable", "unstable", or state that the Stability Theorem is "inconclusive".
You must show your work using the Stability Theorem for credit.
                            </p>
                        </statement>
                    </exercise>
                </page>
            <page>
                <exercise>
                    <statement>
                        <p>
                            Consider the function
<me>
j(x) = 12x^{\frac{1}{3}} - x
</me>.
<ol>
    <li>
